Smoke test for reference-style links and ref-defs.

[doc]: <Marker Fields>
[ext]: https://example.com "External title"
[Case Test]: <Marker Kinds>

## Basic resolution

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `[click here][doc]` | link to Marker Fields | [click here][doc] |
| `[external][ext]` | link to example.com with tooltip "External title" | [external][ext] |

## Case insensitive + whitespace normalized

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `[X][CASE TEST]` | link to Marker Kinds | [X][CASE TEST] |
| `[X][case test]` | link to Marker Kinds | [X][case test] |
| `[X][  case   test  ]` | link to Marker Kinds | [X][  case   test  ] |

## Unresolved → literal

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `[foo][nosuch]` | literal characters `[foo][nosuch]` | [foo][nosuch] |

## Coexistence with inline links

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `[inline](#Marker Fields) and [ref][doc]` | both links resolve | [inline](#Marker Fields) and [ref][doc] |

## Ref-def appears AFTER usage (single-pass limitation)

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `[before-def][late]` then later `[late]: target` | literal — def comes too late | [before-def][late] |

[late]: <Some Tiddler>

The `[late]: <Some Tiddler>` def above appears AFTER its usage in source. The usage above already rendered as literal text. This is the documented single-pass limitation.
